  "worked_solution": "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we sketch the set ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253769/assets/d9a318d9898757b5553c6875afd47a0e38d93a5ecd7fb44a7aaeee5b653358cc.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{p}$ or ${T}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253769/assets/dfb20ade46701d88609c4d1a23d95dd41c3bcceff58ecf3ee6d33095857d7548.png)\n\nAs a result, we get the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253769/assets/d241c79ec2ab5c8ddc6cc4d1cf33f3355a91c44b30661afcf90e39e1b8ff6969.png)",
